        "subject": "LU-20630 tests: compare lnetctl Multi-Rail case-insensitively",
        "message": "LU-20630 tests: compare lnetctl Multi-Rail case-insensitively\n\nlnetctl renders the Multi-Rail flag as \"false\"/\"true\" through the\nNetlink path (LNet genl peer support, 8a0fdfa0b2, 2.16+) but as\n\"False\"/\"True\" through the legacy cYAML path used when the peer's\nkernel does not implement that command.  sanity-lnet test_238 reads\nthe flag from ${ROUTERS[0]}, so a router running 2.15 makes its exact\ncomparison against lowercase \"false\" fail:\n\n  test_238: Expect 'Multi-Rail: false', found False\n\nThe setup_health_test guard compares against \"False\" instead, so the\nfile already disagrees with itself.  Compare both case-insensitively.\n\nFixes: bb6237483d (\"LU-19827 lnet: Fix MR forwarding\")\nFixes: f0be00678c (\"LU-9680 lnet: collect data about peer_ni by using Netlink\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: Iaa601374d0723b5af3c9b8d67ce573baee4ac536\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68266\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
